From f0083199f12a4c0dbf565208ec279cd975da31fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:56:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 51/63] nxhost: stop re-uploading textures the GPU has rendered
 into

A texture first created for sampling is re-uploaded from guest memory
whenever that memory changes. Once the GPU draws or copies into it, its
contents live only in the Metal texture, and a re-upload overwrites them
with the guest's empty or stale bytes. In Splatoon 3's lobby this blacked
out the whole 3D view (final composite: exposure from a 1x1 readback
target, colour grading from an 8x8x8 LUT rendered once per scene).

Diagnostics used to find it: NX_MSL_OVERRIDE=<dir> compiles an edited
<hash>_<extra>.metal instead of the translation; draw dumps report NaN/Inf
pixel counts; NX_TRACE_3D_TARGETS logs draws, copies and CPU uploads into
3D textures; NX_TRACE_3D_TEXTURES reads back sampled 3D textures; failed
texture views are logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013yetZ2nJDh2A6QWpF2QWuu
